==German==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|de|Walnuß||pre-1996}}

===Etymology===
17th century, from {{bor|de|nds|-}}, from {{der|de|gml|walnut}}, from {{der|de|gmw-pro|*walhahnut}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*walhaz|t=foreign}} + {{m|gem-pro|*hnuts|t=nut}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|walnoot}}, {{cog|en|walnut}}, and (from Middle Low German) {{cog|da|valnød}} etc. Equivalent to {{m|de||wal-}} (related with {{m|de|welsch}}) + {{m|de|Nuss}}; compare {{cog|gmh|welhisch nuz}} (alongside {{m|gmh|boumnuz}}). Possibly a {{cal|de|la|nux gallica|nocap=1}}, but the name may merely describe the foreign origin as such; compare {{noncog|fi|saksanpähkinä|lit=German nut}}.

